  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "Only events relevant to ordered object search, claim, approach, pickup, zone search/approach, and drop are included: color observation (object/zone visible, not visible, reached), claim (claim_<color>, received_claim_<color>), motion phase selection (search_object, approach_object, search_zone, approach_zone as required by runtime contract), pick_up_object, and drop_object. All low-level movement and task-level movement commands (task_move_forward, task_rotate_clockwise, task_rotate_counterclockwise) are omitted as these are outside mission protocol decisions and specified to be self-looped only for assignment events; obstacle and unrelated events are omitted per the contract.",
    "transition_design": "States represent protocol steps: searching for any unclaimed object, per-color claim, approach, reacquisition/search, pickup, zone search/approach, and drop. Each color branch is explicit and mutually exclusive, with transitions controlled by appropriate observations and arbitration (received_claim_<color>). repeatable search/approach commands self-loop in the corresponding phase as required. The automaton guarantees that only one object of any color is delivered in each run by marking only the 'finished' state, reachable only by passing through the pickup and drop sequence for a single object/zone pair. Each uncontrollable observation that can affect the mission flow (object/zone visible, not visible, reached, received claim) causes explicit and deterministic transitions to ensure correct sequencing, reacquisition if objects/zones are lost, and arbitration correctness. All required controllable events appear at least once, and disabled events are not included.",
